@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Threat model — untrusted-input dataflow and trust boundaries

' ---- Primary flow: parsing untrusted source bytes -----------------------
start
:untrusted source bytes;<<#FFE3E3>>
:max_file_size guard
(reject > 10 MB in build());<<#D3F9D8>>
note right
  <b>Trust boundary.</b> build_from_tree (Mode B)
  <i>skips</i> this size check — enforcing an input
  bound is then the caller's responsibility.
end note
:tree-sitter parse
(bounded; no code execution);<<#DBE4FF>>
:CPG construction
(AST + CFG + DFG);<<#F1F3F5>>
:bounded analyses —
VF2 max_matches, DFG max_iterations,
slice max_nodes;<<#E5DBFF>>
:results;<<#C3FAE8>>
stop

' ---- Separate flow: deserialization is its own trust boundary ------------
start
:serialized graph bytes (serde feature);<<#FFE3E3>>
:serde deserialization
= trust boundary
(load only trusted graphs);<<#FFE3E3>>
:CodePropertyGraph (trusted only);<<#C3FAE8>>
stop

legend right
  |= colour |= role |
  |<#FFE3E3>| trust boundary / untrusted input |
  |<#D3F9D8>| input-size guard |
  |<#DBE4FF>| bounded parse (no exec) |
  |<#E5DBFF>| bounded analysis |
  |<#C3FAE8>| trusted result |
endlegend
@enduml
